<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21177" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hyperbŏrĕi</span></b> ,
			ōrum, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὑπερβόρεοι</span> (-<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ειοι</span>), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				fabulous people living at the extreme north</i>, <i>the Hyperboreans</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 1,
				2, 4 sq.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">3, 5,
				1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 12, 26, § 89</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. N. D.
				3, 23, 57</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Derivv. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hyper-bŏrĕus</span></b> , a,
				um, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to the Hyperboreans</i>, <i>Hyperborean</i>, <b>poet.</b>, also i. q. <i>northern</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">campi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 2, 20, 16</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">orae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 3, 196</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">glacies,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 4, 517</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pruinae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Fl. 8, 210</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ursa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Luc. 5,
					23</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">septentrio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 3, 381</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pallene,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 15, 356</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">triumphus (gained over the Catti and Dacii),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					8, 78, 3</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hyper-bŏrĕānus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., the same, Hier. ap.
			Chron. Euseb. ad Ann. 1560.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
